scenario: RADIO-EAR-01
title: Radio stations by ear
area: Radio
rows: F-RADIO-01, F-RADIO-02
machines: any
needs: person
prereq: Internet connection and working speakers.
step: Open RADIO and choose a language from the list on the left, then a station.
expect: The station starts playing within ten seconds and the player shows its name.
clause: F-RADIO-02.play
step: Listen for thirty seconds.
expect: The sound is continuous and clean, without dropouts, and the loudness is the same as other sounds on the machine.
clause: F-RADIO-01.quality
step: Press Stop, then Play.
expect: Stopping is immediate, and the station resumes after Play.
clause: F-RADIO-02.stop-play
step: Add a station of your own (a name and a stream address) and play it.
expect: The new station is saved, appears under My stations and plays.
clause: F-RADIO-01.add
